# ID Architecture Contract

Three identities. Never merge them.

- **internal_id** (`mods.internal_id` TEXT): durable business Entity Identity. Answers “is this the same Mod?”. Minted at create; proven on disk as `.info/internal_id` (same value — not a third Mod ID). Never `internal_id = str(mod_id)`. Never `workspace_id`. Never `correlation_id`.
- **mod_id** (`mods.mod_id`): SQLite row PK and FK target only. Not the business Entity Identity. Business callers resolve `internal_id → resolve_mod_pk() → mod_id → DB/FK`.
- **Workspace ID** (`mods.workspace_id`): platform / display identity only (Steam Workshop ID, Nexus Mod ID, …). NEVER Library / Reconcile / Backup / Deploy / UI entity identity. `find_mod_by_workspace_id` is a permanent no-op.
- **external_id**: platform-native metadata. Not a second user Mod ID.

Derivation (never invert):

```
Steam Workshop ID → external_id → workspace_id
Nexus Mod ID     → external_id → workspace_id
Other            → system-generated workspace_id (never from internal_id or mod_id)
```

Forbidden: `workspace_id = internal_id`, `workspace_id = mod_id`, treating `mods.mod_id` as Frozen entity identity, Internal ID in platform URLs, ordinary UI showing Internal ID / Steam Workshop ID / Nexus ID beside Workspace ID.

Steam PK may numerically equal Workshop ID (historical). Same digits ≠ same semantics.

Use names `internal_id`, `mod_id`, `workspace_id`, `external_id`. Do not use ambiguous `mod_id` for more than one of these.

Ordinary UI shows **Workspace ID** only. Debug UI may show **SQLite PK**. `.info/internal_id` is filesystem registration proof (same Entity `internal_id`), not a folder-name identity.

Do not introduce `entity_key` as an identity field. A temporary legacy JSON key named `entity_key` may be read once and migrated to `internal_id`; never write it as canonical.
